From 35631c50f563bc20bcd01987ebcf8441d867b21d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:19:35 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 launch: early window callback before browser
 startup

Launch waits for ready (PostBrowserStart) before the host can show any
window, so the cached sidebar the shell has prepared stays off screen while
Chromium creates its threads, profile and services. ABI 1.45 (early_window,
bridge 0.47.0) adds ReArcEngineSetEarlyWindowCallback, settable between
Configure and Run. Run calls it once, synchronously on the main thread, at
the end of InstallReArcAppDelegateAndMenu (the ReArc branch of
ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::PreCreateThreads): NSApplication, its delegate
and the placeholder menu exist, browser threads and profiles do not, and the
main message loop is not running. The host may create, order front and
flush AppKit windows there; every other ABI call still answers as before
ready. The hook lives in the rearc_bridge source set, so no upstream file
outside framework.exports and framework.order changes. An abi signpost
interval (EarlyWindow) covers the callback. Existing ABI layouts remain
unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-06 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).
---
